f its five categories presupposes the item is already on the line you hand it.** An item that silently **stops** being carried is therefore invisible to it, and it duly reported `CLOSED=0 · OPEN=0 · BOTH=0 · OPEN-DESK-ONLY=16 · UNRECORDED=0` for s1639 — a clean bill — while a 530 MB owner-gated item sat off the desk entirely. **That is F-1471-3's shape one level out: the desk guard fails OPEN, and what it fails open on is the SET, not the spelling.** ⓘ **HONEST LIMIT ON THE GENERALISATION — a screen is not a census, and mine was too crude to support one.** Counting BACKLOG rows whose line STARTS `- 🔺` gives 28 marked rows against 16 carried with only **3** ids in common, which looks alarming; but that key reports its hits and never its misses — **all 13 carried-without-a-🔺-row items DO have rows, under other markers (🟡/🟠/👑) or mid-line.** So the two registries genuinely diverge, but the size of the divergence is **UNMEASURED** and would need an instrument keyed on every marker spelling (the `drain-block-check` lesson: never conclude from one field name). Recorded as a signal worth an instrument, **not** as a measured defect. ✅ **ACTION TAKEN s1640: restored to the desk (16 → 17 carried), with the live numbers.** **GATE: OWNER — unchanged and still one word: salvage to a branch (the s1350 precedent, `save/art-staging-20260801`), accept the loss deliberately, or prune deliberately. No fire may take a 530 MB repo-size decision unilaterally (F-1103-2), and this fire did not.** ⚙️ **UPDATED s1658 (F-1658-1) — THE GATE IS UNCHANGED, BUT ONE OF ITS THREE OPTIONS WAS NOT EXECUTABLE UNTIL TODAY.** `salvage to a branch` names `scripts/salvage-art-staging.mjs`, and that script reached **0 of the 582 at-risk files** — it read only `worktrees/art/assets/raw`, non-recursively, while 100% of the exposure is nested under `motion-pilot/`. Answering *"salvage it"* would have produced a `save/*` branch holding 3 irrelevant files and a success line. **Fixed and guarded `c5d077cec` (8/8