# e1-baron attempt — prime-r1

## Pre-run hypothesis

The prior best treated palisades as a long blocking wall and spent its boss reserve repairing remote wrecks while too few guns could reach the Baron. I will instead finish the actual damage engine before wave 20: three income sluices, all four turrets at tier III in a tight north-bank kill box, six nearby beacons, and an offense-weighted thirty-pick draft. At wave 19 I will add separated 10-gold palisades as disposable rocket/strike decoys, with only the first narrow center panel intercepting the ford. Its wave-scaled HP should fall just below 31% after a 128-damage Baron strike, so `REPAIR_UNDER 31` deterministically selects it without paying for ordinary scratches. Between damage/repair observations, brief `blast`→`rig` standing-order pairs should fire an auto-aimed Blast Charge while keeping the Spark Rig active; an explicit cooldown refusal creates the next deterministic observation.

This differs from the failed line-and-stockpile plan by concentrating every capped gun inside the boss stop point, maxing turret tiers before luxury economy, and using cheap, separated shot decoys rather than a remote fortification line.

