scripts/tmp-s1178-handoff.mjs:5:const HANDOFF = `Last updated: 2026-07-28T18:29Z s1178 handoff, lock CLEARED — **I WAS SENT TO A BOARD LABELLED PIPELINE-DRY ON FIVE SLOTS. IT WAS NOT DRY — THE SECOND-LARGEST RED CLUSTER ON THE BOARD HAD NO LEDGER LINE AT ALL, AND THE THING THAT NAMED ITS CAUSE WAS THE TWO CASES THAT *PASSED*.** **(A) ⓘ NO DRAIN WAS AVAILABLE AND I DID NOT MANUFACTURE ONE.** lane-c was LIVE on \`eight-winds-wiring-hero\` (picked up 17:58:02, log growing), \`tasks/done/\` held nothing newer than s1177's own merge, all five other queues empty, no \`CODEX-WALL\`. Tracked dirt was **only** the carried \`artifacts/\` + \`logs/\` churn — **zero \`src/\`** — so nothing was drainable and nothing was mine to commit. **(B) ✍️ AUTHORED + QUEUED → lane-a, and the runner PICKED IT UP AT 18:28:40 — lane-a is LIVE.** \`tasks/lane-a-cp04-lever-unlock-seed-realign.md\` (\`831a8ea5\`; goal leaf \`factory-cp04-lever-unlock-seed-realign\` + the BACKLOG line in the **same commit**). ✓ I verified the *running* copy is my committed master by **hash**, not by assumption: \`727f7e7a2d1a2943\` on both. **(C) 🟠 F-1178-1 — THE DEFECT, AND IT WAS INVISIBLE TO THE LEDGER.** \`grep -c "cp04" tasks/BACKLOG.md\` = **0**; \`goals.json\` held only the **merged** CP-04 leaf. **16 red executions** — \`cp04-lever.spec.ts:146\` × 7 seeded boots × 2 projects = **14**, plus \`:106\` × 2 — counted **row-by-row out of \`logs/suite-red-inventory.md:65-80\`**, not inherited. That is **5.3% of the 303-row board, the second-largest single-file cluster**, behind only the eight \`town-*-blender\` specs already owner-gated as F-1167-1. **Both sites are \`toHaveText\`, NOT timeouts ⇒ F-1167-2's discount does not apply**; masking **83–87%** means they die early and most of their steps never run. **(D) 🔑 THE DISCRIMINATOR WAS ALREADY SITTING IN THE DATA AND COST ONE PASS OF ARITHMETIC.** \`bootSample\` (\`:25\`) is \`[0,4,17,10,23,24,29,30,43]\` = **NINE** boots, but only **SEVEN** are red. Decomposing each index as \`land*9+story*3+visitors\` against \`LEVER_LANDS\` order: **indices 0 and 4 are BOTH \`the-claim\`, and BOTH are green**; all seven non-\`the-claim\` boots are red. **A perfect split that has nothing to do with story or visitors** — and \`:106\` obeys the same rule (it presses through on \`e1-twin-banks\`). **\`the-claim\` is \`DEFAULT_CONTRACT_ID\`** (\`ContractFamilies.ts:701\`). **(E) ⚠️ THE SUSPECT IS STATED AS A SUSPECT, BECAUSE I DID NOT RUN THE SPEC** — lane-c owned the box and lane worktrees share port 5188 (Mistake #12). \`src/meta/ContractUnlock.ts\` **did not exist** when this spec shipped (\`d21cac4e\`, 07-17, whose own commit message records *"cp04 24/24 both projects"*); it arrived **07-23** in \`6c009cb8\` (+92, *"feat: add physical E1 release build"*). \`contractUnlockStatus:17-45\` returns unlocked immediately **only** for \`unlock === "default"\`; everything else is conditional on scoreboard rows, research state, or an active epoch — **and \`cp04-lever\` seeds none of them** (two \`sessionStorage\` keys, then navigate; \`localStorage\` virgin). ✓ **THE CONTROL PROVES THE GATE'S OWN AUTHOR KNEW THIS:** \`e2e/release-build.spec.ts\`, authored **in that same commit**, never navigates without \`seedProfile(page, { unlocked: true })\` (\`:99\`,\`:109\`,\`:132\`,\`:167\`,\`:186\`), and that helper (\`:202-245\`) seeds **exactly what the gate reads** — scores with \`secured: true\` for \`the-claim\` **and** \`e1-dry-gulch\`, \`activeEpoch\`, the meta science track, the research \`taken\` list — plus a deliberate **locked** arm at \`:177\`. ➡️ **The F-1170-2 shape exactly: a commit adds a gate, writes its OWN spec that respects it, and updates none of the pre-existing specs that don't.** **(F) 🛡️ HOW THE MASTER IS BUILT SO IT CANNOT INSTALL A FALSE GREEN.** Scope 1 is a **mandatory observe-the-defect STOP** capturing the expected-vs-actual string pair **plus \`activeId\`**, classifying **(a) silent fallback to the default** vs **(b) something else** — **(b) STOPS, and an already-green tree STOPS too** (the inventory is 02:26Z; something may have landed). ⛔ **All \`src/**\` firewalled with a STOP instruction rather than an edit** — the unlock gate is **shipped, ratified E1-release behaviour**, and a cure that edits it reverses a merged release decision. The cure may **not** weaken either assertion to a regex/substring/\`toContainText\`: the spec's value is that it cross-checks **two independent code paths** (the charter composer vs the HUD briefing, \`src/ui/Hud.ts:329\`). \`"a plain boot remains inert"\` (\`:117-127\`) keeps its **virgin storage** — that IS its point. Mutation control aims at the **SUBJECT** (drop one boot's seed, show the same surface returns, restore and re-prove). **F-1173-5 folded in:** \`--workers=1\` mandated and the worker count must be **stated**. \`release-build\`'s own 14 reds are firewalled and **expected to stay red** (\`:160\`/\`:107\`/\`:199\`, fingerprint \`:192-197\`). **(G) 🔺 A POSSIBLE OWNER FORK IS PRE-DECLARED, NOT PRE-DECIDED.** If scope 1 lands on (a), then a fresh save opening the Charter Press Lever is offered **five** lands and can launch **one** — the other four silently boot The Claim. Whether the Lever should hide locked lands, show them locked, or unlock-on-press is an **owner design fork**; the master orders it **written up and reported, explicitly NOT fixed** (§2E hard limit). But per s1170's lesson I did **not** park the whole item behind it — the test-side realign is fire-authorable today and does not wait on the ruling. **(H) ✓ LANE-SAFETY PROVED BY THE UNIQUE-BLOB INVARIANT, NOT THE AHEAD-COUNT.** \`lane/m3\` is 1 ahead at \`ced4484f\` whose content shipped as \`011e85fc\`; \`git diff --name-only --diff-filter=A main..lane/m3\` is **EMPTY** ⇒ the lane holds **zero** files main lacks, so the runner's reset destroys nothing. Routed to lane-a because \`lane/m4\` and \`lane/perf\` each uniquely hold a file absent from main, and lane-c was LIVE. **(I) 🧾 DUTIES.** **ART audit NOT owed** — I did not refill, drain, or process the ART slot. **ASSAYER \`pending/\` = 0** (listed, empty). **GAZETTE — no item; filter law working: I merged nothing.** **TK-01 NOT owed, re-derived at the file's own header:** \`ticker-digest-2026-07-27.md:1\` reads *"compiled s1154 fire 2026-07-28 06:0x local"* ⇒ the 07-28 digest is owed after 06:00 on **07-29**. **DEPLOY SKIPPED** — nothing merged, nothing gameplay-affecting. **BACKUP PUSHED: \`e3afb19a..831a8ea5\`.** **GUARDS: \`goal-tracker\` 2/2 green after the goals.json edit · \`task-guard-audit\` 686→687 masters, 0 invisible · \`drain-block-check --queue\` ✅ CLEAR before the \`cp\`.** **(J) ➡️ NEXT FIRE, IN ORDER: (1) DRAIN whichever of the TWO LIVE LANES lands first — lane-c \`eight-winds-wiring-hero\` (started 17:58) and lane-a \`cp04-lever-unlock-seed-realign\` (started 18:28).** For **lane-c**: read its scope-1 confirmation (three premises), check the scope-2 control shows **\`0 unexplained\`, EXIT=0**, and **if it STOPPED at \`:91\` again, read F-1177-3 before believing it** — the gate text is now correct, so a stop there means something genuinely new; assert **zero \`src/\`** and \`frames.json\` **32 cells, 0 empty**. For **lane-a**: the verdict lives in scope 1(d) — **a well-evidenced (b) or an already-green tree is a LAWFUL STOP, not a failure**; assert \`git status --porcelain -- src/\` is **EMPTY** (an \`src/\` edit is a reject, not a bonus) and that neither \`toHaveText\` was weakened. **(2)** F-1174-1 still needs one owner word on the guard vocabulary (rec: add \`deferred\`) — **two live instances behind it.** **(3)** ⓘ **PIPELINE-DRY: lane-b / lane-d / main / art** — my one-master-per-fire is spent. ⛔ **lane-b must NOT be reset** (\`lane/m4\`) and **lane-d must NOT be reset** (\`lane/perf\`, F-1167-3): **both RE-PROVEN this fire by content**, each uniquely holds a file absent from main. **(K) 🧹 I killed nothing, started no servers, ran no Playwright, and merged nothing.** Read-only probes plus three guard runs; the \`artifacts/\` + \`logs/\` churn is untouched and still the owner's keep-or-revert call. **(L) OWNER'S DESK — no new decision yet** (F-1178-1's fork is *conditional* on scope 1 landing on (a); it is flagged, not filed). 🔻 **F-1174-1** one word on guard vocabulary (two live instances) · 🔺 **F-1173-2** rec (a) · 🔺 **F-1169-5** E9 town portraits — four faces read as one woman · 🔺 **F-1167-1** rec (a) · 🔺 **F-1167-3** >100 MB Playwright raw can never reach origin · 🔺 **F-1166-1** jumper 8-way, rec (a) · 🔺 **F-1141-3 + F-1164-1 — ONE decision at \`+240px\` (\`src/styles.css:1620\`) closes TWO reds** · 🔺 **F-1162-1 — RESTART THE LANE RUNNER** (14th instance) · 🔺 \`DRAFT-e1-hold-the-claim\` · \`DRAFT-e1-trail-guide-plain-boot-proof\` · \`autosprite-trial-gate\` (needs credits) · 🔁 **F-1161-3** rec (a) · 🔁 \`lane-a-m3-05-run-history\` re-scope · 🔁 \`011\` §3+§5 re-scope · 🔁 **F-1044-3** E9 \`bld-*\` adjudication · 🔁 \`.wrangler\` untracking · 🔁 \`artifacts/\` churn keep-or-revert · **F-1120-2 AT RISK 566.47 MB** (carried, NOT re-measured — I did not touch the ART slot) · **F-1103-2** the \`*.log\` retention hole · **calibrate-suite-workers-v2** environment-blocked · carried: F-1147-1 + F-1148-1 · F-1147-2 · F-1144-2 · F-1141-2 · E① F-1131-5 · E② F-1130-6 · F-1123-4 · ⚠️ \`tasks/art-e9-buildings-a.md\` still carries no \`⛔\` header despite \`BACKLOG:963\`. **(M) THE LESSON — s1177 taught that a cure invalidates the gate TEXT its callers were written against. The completion is that A "DRY BOARD" IS A CLAIM ABOUT THE QUEUES, AND QUEUES ARE NOT WHERE WORK LIVES.** Five slots read PIPELINE-DRY and every queue dir really was empty — yet the second-largest red cluster on the board had been failing for days with **zero** lines in BACKLOG and **zero** leaves in \`goals.json\`. It was never *blocked*; it was **never written down**, so no ladder could offer it and no dry-check could see it. ➡️ **Concretely: when the queues are dry, stop auditing the ladders and audit the MEASURED ARTEFACTS instead** — here, one pass over \`logs/suite-red-inventory.md\` clustering by file. And once you have a cluster, **find the siblings that DON'T fail**: two of nine boots were green, nobody had asked why, and that single question produced the mechanism, the suspect commit, and the in-repo control — before a single test was run.`;
